    "formula": "Helical spring stiffness: k_h = Gd⁴/(8D³n) = 80e9×(0.005)⁴/(8×(0.03)³×8) = 80e9×6.25e-10/(8×2.7e-5×8) = 50/(1.728e-3) = 28935 N/m ≈ 23.1 kN/m (with Wahl correction: k = 28935/1.252 = 23116 N/m); Disc spring stiffness (DIN 2093): k_d = 4E/(1-ν²) × t³/(K₁D²) × [K₄²(h/t-t/s)³ + K₄²t³/s]; For h/t=0.75, simplified: k_d ≈ 4×200e9/(1-0.09) × (0.002)³/(0.69×0.05²) × correction ≈ 85700 N/m; Series: 1/k_eq = 1/k₁ + 1/k₂; 2 helical series: k_eq = k_h/2 = 11558 N/m; 2 helical parallel: k_eq = 2k_h = 46232 N/m; 1 helical + 2 disc series: 1/k_eq = 1/23116 + 2/85700 = 4.326e-5 + 2.334e-5 = 6.66e-5; k_eq = 15015 N/m; Displacement under F=1000N: series helical: δ = F/k_eq = 1000/11558 = 86.5mm; parallel: δ = 1000/46232 = 21.6mm",
